# Cornie Frontend Rules

## Component Reuse
- ALWAYS prefer existing neobrutalism-vue components before writing custom ones.
- ALWAYS prefer lucide-vue icons before creating custom icons.
- NEVER write a component from scratch if a neobrutalism-vue equivalent exists.
- All project-specific reusable components go into src/renderer/components/.

## Forbidden: Descriptive Copy
- NEVER include feature description text in cards, headers, or any UI element.
- NO marketing copy, NO feature explanations, NO "about" text anywhere.
- Module cards show ONLY: icon + title + badge. No description paragraph.
- Greetings are limited to time-based short phrases only (e.g., "上午好").

## Forbidden: Emoji
- NEVER use emoji characters (🐐 📖 🧠 🔍 💰 ✅ 📅 ⚙️ etc.) in any Vue component.
- ALL icons MUST come from @lucide/vue.
- If a Lucide icon does not exist, use the closest available alternative.

## Code Style
- No comments in Vue components or JavaScript unless documenting a non-obvious workaround.
- Use `<script setup>` exclusively.
- Prefer composition over configuration.
- Import only what is used; avoid barrel imports that pull in unused code.